menu "BME688 air quality (BSEC)"

    config BME688_USE_BSEC
        bool "Enable Bosch BSEC air-quality fusion for BME688"
        default n
        help
            Compile the BSEC integration that turns the BME688 raw gas signal
            into IAQ / CO2-equivalent / breath-VOC-equivalent outputs. Requires
            the proprietary Bosch BSEC library and headers to be installed under
            components/bsec2/bosch/ (see components/bsec2/README.md). The library
            is NOT redistributable and is therefore not committed to this
            repository. When disabled the firmware builds with no air-quality
            outputs and no external dependency.

    config BME688_BSEC_SAMPLE_RATE_ULP
        bool "Use ULP (~300 s) sample rate instead of LP (~3 s)"
        depends on BME688_USE_BSEC
        default n
        help
            LP (low power, ~3 s cycle) gives responsive IAQ at higher power draw.
            ULP (ultra-low power, ~300 s) minimises power for battery use at the
            cost of responsiveness.

    config BME688_BSEC_STATE_SAVE_INTERVAL_MIN
        int "BSEC calibration-state save interval (minutes, 0 = never)"
        depends on BME688_USE_BSEC
        default 60
        help
            How often the BSEC calibration state is persisted to NVS so the gas
            baseline and accuracy survive reboots. State is only saved once BSEC
            reports high accuracy.

endmenu
